{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32418-how-are-the-dragon-age-books","id":32418,"title":"How are the Dragon Age Books?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-18T08:26:05-08:00","id":32418,"title":"How are the Dragon Age Books?","content":"Okay so I got into Dragon Age well after the 2nd game was long out and I loved the friggin setting! Then I hear I think Green Ronin made Dragon Age RPG books, how are they? Has anyone read them and or played them? I'm interested and I want to know how it worked out. What system does it use? I love the various whitewolf systems myself so I would probably be inclined to just port it to a system I like and am more familiar with :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T08:28:37-08:00","id":32423,"title":"","content":"Okay found it on <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/68991/Dragon-Age-RPG-Set-1?term=dragon+age?affiliate_id=11894\" target=\"_blank\">Drivethru</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T09:15:51-08:00","id":32462,"title":"","content":"They played it on Tabletop if you're interested <a href=\"http://youtu.be/Y-61i3R5y9Y\" target=\"_blank\">http://youtu.be/Y-61i3R5y9Y</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T09:22:38-08:00","id":32467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solomon birch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32418-how-are-the-dragon-age-books?p=32462#post32462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They played it on Tabletop if you're interested <a href=\"http://youtu.be/Y-61i3R5y9Y\" target=\"_blank\">http://youtu.be/Y-61i3R5y9Y</a></div> </div> </div> </div> I saw that, they even linked that on Drivethru! I am about to watch it, just finishing up the Darker Days I'm listening to first. What is Tabletop though? It has a lot of minor celebrities in that ep. Is it a Youtube series or a podcast?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T09:45:56-08:00","id":32491,"title":"","content":"It's a show on a site called Geek &amp; Sundry. Wil Wheaton plays boardgames with people (some internet famous, some just friends and family). I find it funny. I remembered that episode because it had the guy from the American Being Human on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T11:55:23-08:00","id":32609,"title":"","content":"I have read the Player's Guide and Game Master's Guide, though only set I (which only covers the first 5 levels of character advancement). It has its own system - though I have seem some mentions on the net of it being called the Age System, so maybe there is something out there that also uses it? Here are the basics of character creation and how the system handles doing stuff:<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b>: You have 8 Abilities: Communication, Constitution, Cunning, Dexterity, Magic, Perception, Strength and Willpower.<br /> <br /> Each Ability starts at a value from -2 to 4 and are assigned via rolling 3D6 for each Ability then comparing to a table which gives the value. After you roll all of them, you can swap the values of any two Abilities. During the rest of character creation, these may increase. you may also get Focuses.<br /> <br /> <b>Focus</b>: A narrower field of expertise within an Ability. They are similar to Attribute Specialties in White Wolf/Onyx Path games and makes your Ability count as two higher when doing stuff related to your Focus. The book has several for each Ability. Examples include:<br /> Communication (Bargaining, Disguise, Leadership), Constitution (Drinking, Running, Stamina), Cunning (Heraldry, Musical Lore. Navigation), Dexterity (Acrobatics, Caligraphy, Traps), Magic (Entropy, Primal, Spirit), Perception (Empathy, Hearing, Tracking), Strength (Intimidation, Jumping, Spears), Willpower (Faith, Courage, Self-Discipline)<br /> <br /> You customize you character by selecting:<br /> <br /> - <b>Background</b>: a combination of Race and social circumstances - Includes stuff like &quot;Circle Mage&quot; or &quot;City Elf&quot;. Each grants +1 to a specific Ability, a Focus from a small list, one or more Languages, some class restrictions and two rolls on a table, with each roll giving +1 to an Ability or a specific Focus)<br /> <br /> - <b>Class</b>: Mage, Rogue or Warrior. They determine your Health, the Weapon Groups you know how to use (choices are involved if you are a Warrior), especial powers of a given Class (Such as a Mage's magic) and some choices for your starting Talents<br /> - <b>Talents</b>: Special training or aptitudes. Stuff like Animal Training, Music, Command, Contacts, various Weapon Styles, Types of Magic, Thievery and so on. On the set 1 they can be Novice or Journeyman. I assume further sets have greater advancements<br /> <br /> - <b>Equipment</b>: standard package with some variation depending on your Class and Weapon Groups, plus some currency to buy additional stuff<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ability Tests</b>: Basic tests are 3D6 + Ability + Focus, trying to reach a given target number. Some tasks may not be attempted if you don't have that focus, others you can do with only the Ability. Opposed tests are the same, but two or more people rolling against each other's result instead of a fixed target number<br /> <br /> Of the 3 rolled dice, one is a different color, called a <i>Dragon dice</i>, and serves several functions: measuring degree of success (when it matters how well you succeed at something, the higher the value of the Dragon Dice, the better you do. 1 = barely pulled it off, 6 = did it flawlessly), breaking ties, generating stunt points in combat (Stunts are sort of &quot;special maneuver&quot; you can perform, like Disarm, Knock Prone, Rapid Reload or Dual Strike. Using Stunts costs Stunt Points)<br /> <br /> <b>Spells</b>: they consume Mana (which only Mages have), and require a Casting Test using the Magic Ability (and Focus on that type of Magic if you have it) against that spell's target number. Rolling exceptionally well may allow you to perform especial Spell Stunts. Some spells allow targets to try to resist them, rolling (something described in the spell) against your Spellpower, which is 10+Magic+Focus (if applicable).<br /> <br /> <b>Attack and Damage</b>: Attacks are Basic Ability Tests of the Appropriate Ability+ Focus (such as Strength + Heavy Blades or Dexterity + Bows) + other bonuses (aiming, charging, magic items, Talents, etc) against the target number of the opponents Defense (10+Dexterity+Shield Bonus).<br /> <br /> Damage is Weapon Damage (value depends on the weapon used) + Strength (except the Bow Weapon Group, which uses Perception instead) + other Modifiers (such as Talents or Magic) - the Armor Rating of the opponent. The result is subtracted from their Health. Most NPCs die when health reaches zero. PCs and some important NPCs stay dying for 2+ Constitution Rounds, and die after that unless they receive healing in that time.<br /> <br /> I think this covers all the basics","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}